2026-11-22 20:08:34 - Agent_20261122200618 - INFO - [+] Agent signaled completion: Reviewed CodeQL SSRF results for jsonschema's network-fetch sink. Confirmed that `_RefResolver.resolve_remote` performs unrestricted fetches of attacker-controllable `$ref`/base_uri values: (1) `requests.get(uri).json()` at line 1221 — protocol/host not restricted beyond being in handlers or http/https, allowing internal-network SSRF and response leakage via JSON parse (or error messages); (2) `urlopen(uri)` at line 1228 — the fallback path for any other scheme (file://, ftp://, gopher://, etc.) enabling local file read (file:// /etc/passwd) and access to internal services, with the `# noqa: S310` comment confirming the bandit warning was knowingly suppressed; (3) the deprecated `_warn_for_remote_retrieve` helper at line 108-113 which retrieves arbitrary remote references via `urlopen` inside the default `_REMOTE_WARNING_REGISTRY`, meaning even the "new" referencing-based flow auto-fetches remote refs without any allowlist. Exploit paths reach these sinks from untrusted schemas via `resolve()`/`resolve_from_url()` (line 1122) and from the CLI `--base-uri` argument (cli.py:272). Also noted `_RefResolver` is deprecated and handlers/cache can be supplied by callers, but that does not mitigate SSRF in default usage. Submitted 3 true-positive findings (lines 1221, 1228, 108).
